{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":37.40999984741211,"text":"Around the Parthenon ran a frieze 160 meters long, a marble ribbon showing a procession—riders, chariots, musicians, girls carrying gifts, cattle for the sacrifice—all on their way to the festival of Athena. In this room you see the horses rearing and the young riders holding them, so alive you can almost hear the hooves. Lord Elgin took them down from the temple between 1801 and 1812, and Britain bought them in 1816. The rest of the frieze is in the Acropolis Museum, with white plaster copies standing in for the pieces that are here.","words":[{"word":"Around","start":0,"end":0.6399999856948853},{"word":"the","start":0.6399999856948853,"end":1.0199999809265137},{"word":"Parthenon","start":1.0199999809265137,"end":1.399999976158142},{"word":"ran","start":1.399999976158142,"end":1.7000000476837158},{"word":"a","start":1.7000000476837158,"end":2.3399999141693115},{"word":"frieze","start":2.3399999141693115,"end":2.3399999141693115},{"word":"160","start":2.3399999141693115,"end":3.700000047683716},{"word":"meters","start":3.700000047683716,"end":4.099999904632568},{"word":"long","start":4.099999904632568,"end":4.5},{"word":"a","start":4.980000019073486,"end":5.139999866485596},{"word":"marble","start":5.139999866485596,"end":5.400000095367432},{"word":"ribbon","start":5.400000095367432,"end":5.71999979019165},{"word":"showing","start":5.71999979019165,"end":6.119999885559082},{"word":"a","start":6.119999885559082,"end":6.420000076293945},{"word":"procession—riders","start":6.420000076293945,"end":7.78000020980835},{"word":"chariots","start":8.5,"end":8.5600004196167},{"word":"musicians","start":9.119999885559082,"end":9.279999732971191},{"word":"girls","start":10,"end":10.319999694824219},{"word":"carrying","start":10.319999694824219,"end":10.680000305175781},{"word":"gifts","start":10.680000305175781,"end":11.079999923706055},{"word":"cattle","start":11.880000114440918,"end":11.880000114440